    "bottomLine": "The Onix Graphite Z5 is the most forgiving single paddle here, with a widebody face retailers list at about 15.5 x 8.3 inches and a 7.5 to 8.2 oz mid weight."
  },
  {
    "id": "head-radical-elite",
    "name": "HEAD Radical Elite Pickleball Paddle",
    "badge": "Softest Feel",
    "category": "Widebody, 15mm Core, Fiberglass Composite Face",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "description": "The Radical Elite suits beginners who come from tennis or who simply want a paddle that feels soft and easy. HEAD lists it at 230 grams, about 8.1 ounces, with a 15mm standard core, a fiberglass composite hitting surface and a widebody shape, plus a standard 130mm (5.1-inch) handle. Fiberglass faces tend to feel springy and give easy power with a short swing, and the 15mm core sits between the lively thin cores and the very soft 16mm control paddles, which makes it a balanced first paddle. HEAD describes the widebody shape as giving a larger sweet spot in a shorter, more maneuverable frame. HEAD's regional sites list it at roughly 60 to 70 in local currency, and some regions show it out of stock, so confirm availability and the current US price before you set your heart on it. It is not the cheapest paddle here, but it is the one that will feel the most comfortable for the widest range of new players.",
    "pros": [
      "Listed at 230 g (about 8.1 oz), a classic mid weight",
      "15mm core balances pop and control",
      "Fiberglass composite face gives easy power, per HEAD",
      "Widebody shape with a larger sweet spot"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Several regional HEAD sites list it out of stock",
      "US price not confirmed on HEAD's pages we found",
      "Fiberglass grit wears faster than raw carbon"
