    "description": "JOOLA makes the paddles many of the pros play, and the Essentials set is its entry point. Retailer listings give a paddle weight of about 8.2 ounces, a 12mm Response honeycomb polymer core, a fiberglass face, a 15.5 by 7.9 inch shape and a ridge grip around 4.75 inches long and about 4 inches in circumference. The set includes two paddles, two Primo balls and a sling bag, and the paddles are listed as USA Pickleball approved. The 8.2-ounce weight is the heaviest of our set picks, which gives a little more stability on blocks, and the fiberglass face adds easy pop. Two things to know: the 4-inch grip is on the small side for larger hands, though an overgrip fixes that cheaply, and listed prices ran from about $59.95 for a single paddle to $129.95 for the full set, which puts the set slightly above our budget at full price. Watch for a sale, or buy two single paddles if that works out cheaper.",
