            The best pickleball paddle for most beginners is the <strong class="text-white">Selkirk SLK Neo 2.0 set</strong>, which Pickleheads lists at $79.99 for two 7.5-ounce paddles, four balls and a bag. If you only need one paddle, the <strong class="text-white">Onix Graphite Z5</strong> has the most forgiving widebody face here, and the <strong class="text-white">HEAD Radical Elite</strong> is the softest, most balanced feel.
          </p>
